  "tweets": [
    {
      "text": "To my knowledge, $CRDO doesn't have in-house CW DFB laser manufacturing capabilities, so not quite... \n\nDustphotonics integrates external CW lasers so Credo is another potential $MRVL for the need to M&A laser companies.  \n\nThey did another with Hyperlume earlier but that was for microLEDs, not CW. Lot of industry channel checks like Largan cast a lot of doubts over that microLED commercialization for CPO (not every short reach application).",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2117259390185345372",
      "time": "2026-11-02 22:15",
      "cashtags": [
        "CRDO",
        "MRVL"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$LITE standalone would likely be up on earnings after their new $5B CPO/NPO announcement (separate from $NVDA).\n\nThe margins on that are likely 60%+… which shows how profitable laser players would be at scale.\n\n(Greensboro alone would be $5B revenue/year)\n\nIn terms of the $MRVL deal:\n\n- Extremely positive for Marvell strategically. Also makes remaining laser players very valuable \n\n- $LITE shareholders can cry though about the 1+ year overhang until deal goes through in 2028. \n\nThere’s less independent price discovery as well since a lot of it will be pegged around 4.5 Marvell shares : 1\n\n- I ",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2117296667108278605",
      "time": "2026-11-03 00:43",
      "cashtags": [
        "LITE",
        "MRVL",
        "NVDA"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "@Ericbaofu 中国其实早就有类似 $MRVL 收购 $LITE 的案例了，比如东山精密收购索尔思光电。\n\n不过国内监管环境不太一样，更多还是为了发展自主技术，减少对西方供应链的依赖。\n\n剑桥科技也是个例子，投资了不少国内激光器厂商，来保障供应和扩充产能。\n\n我觉得这次收购对中际旭创和新易盛的战略影响不会太大",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2117262767040463102",
      "time": "2026-11-02 22:29",
      "cashtags": [
        "LITE",
        "MRVL"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "@aleabitoreddit I think CRDO deserves a shout out here",
      "url": "https://x.com/steeluu/status/2117256455178932463",
      "time": "2026-11-02 22:04",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "@aleabitoreddit hello，我是一个你的中国粉丝。你认为这次并购对中国的模块厂会有什么影响吗？比如中际旭创，新易盛。期待你的回复",
      "url": "https://x.com/Ericbaofu/status/2117255917339382033",
      "time": "2026-11-02 22:02",
      "cashtags": [],
      "is_retweet": true
    },
    {
      "text": "Following the Lumentum / Marvell deal: \n\nMy opinion is that independent Western laser players, like $AAOI, $COHR, and $SIVE became a lot more strategically valuable. \n\n$MTSI and $SMTC should get some attention too as emerging laser players in 2027. \n\nIf I had to guess: \n\n1. Companies competing against Marvell, or not in the $NVDA ecosystem bandwagon, such as $AMD, are likely going to rethink their relationship with $LITE.\n\nIf getting bottlenecked by Nvidia capacity agreements wasn't enough... Incentives around qualifying + bringing up other laser players, seems very necessary now. \n\nSince you ",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2117255303301612014",
      "time": "2026-11-02 21:59",
      "cashtags": [
        "AAOI",
        "AMD",
        "COHR",
        "JBL",
        "LITE",
        "MRVL",
        "MTSI",
        "NVDA",
        "SIVE.ST",
        "SMTC"
      ],
      "is_retweet": false
    },
    {
      "text": "@jacobsimon2002 Well.. that was before $MRVL crashed. The deal is 4.5x Marvell shares for every Lumentum share. \n\n4.5x * 196 = $882 (floating), so you're getting that for $LITE, which is still more than current prices.  \n\nIf Marvell recovers, so does Lumentum shares now",
      "url": "https://x.com/aleabitoreddit/status/2117233515104464961",
      "time": "2026-11-02 20:33",
      "cashtags": [
        "LITE",
